n angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(3,-2)$\n- **II.** $(-5,0)$\n- **III.** $(5,2)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi /2},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(3,-2),(-5,0),(5,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256521 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f6a5209-1dd7-5528-9bd5-5bc7fb3d7b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462019} {:answer/id #uuid "e85d203a-19e9-56f3-ac3a-c0e656286c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462020} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6db83a-49a3-58ae-bedd-1966d3e3fe74" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e74dce9-fc12-5890-b1ba-090c92c360ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462021} {:answer/id #uuid "934072a1-cc59-57ad-b108-ba577635684a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/te