"false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469348} :answer-field/id #uuid "81d9abd9-b8ca-5470-8dbb-280bbbd3ab7b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470286}] :question/id #uuid "0d05b255-e15a-5a84-a441-46629f916127" :question/math-academy-id "q-8394" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,0),(1,5),(2,3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(-5,1)$\n- **II.** $(0,-2)$\n- **III.** $(2,-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi /2},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(0,0),(-5,1),(-3,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3d3e243-980a-5443-b39f-968258eea1dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469350} {:answer/id #uuid "b293378d-5abc-5d1a-95f9-ffaf61440ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.ty