e coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(0,0),(0,-2),(2,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b1db85-9532-5e13-8d24-4a7f748e42c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469368} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d78c50-3999-500f-b626-79723927998f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469368} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd234d1c-591d-5d0f-b979-4c49a9efcc6e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470296} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a272b445-6d6b-5af6-bc3b-c488edad75b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469370} {:answer/id #uuid "3a2a9cd5-8e05-5809-bba9-5d3c4a64b972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469370} :answer-field/id #uuid "56019eeb-07b7-5fec-818c-5f47a4dff545" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2958658a-eddd-55ed-b549-021a13283641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469372} {:answer/id #uuid "94763f3c-c5f4-5231-b406-029180e46fff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469373} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c5140c3-3c7a-5ed6-911a-cd2fa6d36d82" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470298}] :question/id #uuid "393a348f-a234-528b-b073-1f1b828e454e" :question/math-academy-id "q-8427" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,2),(-1,2),(-1,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n- **I.** $(1,-1)$\n- **II.** $(0,-2)$\n- **III.** $(-2,-1)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-2,0),(-2,-1),(0,-1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420105 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c4d9e7-fcc1-51cb-9feb-d14eed398feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472754} {:answer/id #uuid "48e4a354-249b-5ba2-9117-b2967ef925f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472755} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd5de993-b98b-510c-aca5-b262d4fe57ab" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/t