0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(3,1),(2,2),(-4,-1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092066 :question/id #uuid "e945271e-2180-559b-9998-53ab9982043c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5458" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(2,-1), (-3,5),$ and $(4,-3).$  Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of $S',$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation $\\mathbf{R}_{\\pi}$ by an angle of $\\pi$ radians about the origin?\n\n- $(-2,1)$\n\n- $(-4,3)$\n\n- $(-5,3)$" :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation $\\mathbf{R}_{\\pi}$ by an angle of $\\pi$ radians is given by the matrix\n\n![](images/a5/a5b5bd722e0f84e175af70516d25edbcdbe55b48cbbb0ee7821d03272afac1ff.svg)\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of $\\mathbf{R}_{\\pi},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S$ as columns:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $\\mathbf{R}_{\\pi}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $S'$ are $(-2,1), (3,-5), (-4,3).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f578c6e-f41b-5a04-82b6-cc05ad3221aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459455} {:answer/id #uuid "19936b31-b905-51ba-91bd-1ea1912b6c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459456} :answer-field/id #uuid "594fe546-4a64-5192-bbba-88d66205aa65" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16790a0a-b686-56e4-b162-fcf03d45fce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459457} {:answer/id #uuid "9c542df2-155c-501f-872a-a77ab69327a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459458} :answer-field/id #uuid "afaf43df-d5b0-5531-b0ec-7ad36dccc91c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460595} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ec105b6-780f-5848-84be-2129f1293f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459459} {:answer/id #uuid "7580c798-5c60-5614-8c7a-4cbdc45e7f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459460} :answer-field/id #uuid "7abbb5d7-793f-5155-8db3-3280754b98ec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460596}] :question/id #uuid "ac0c7623-4587-52d5-8de6-ad1d378c8244" :question/math-academy-id "q-12121" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,-2),(-1,2),(1,1).$  Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(1,2)$\n- **II.** $(1,-2)$\n- **III.** $(-1,-1)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is the same as counterclockwise rotation by the same angle. It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(1,2),(1,-2),(-1,-1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092844 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9c4af76-1cc0-5af1-bed2-5738a3bcd223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091265} {:answer/id #uuid "17e38fa2-ab05-5110-a95b-358c7c84fce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :ans