}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(5,-1),(0,4),(-3,-5).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc15f59-c768-5320-9ec4-70f3d142b675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469266} {:answer/id #uuid "5187f972-9f94-5165-af76-273d295ea3ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469266} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfe89ca2-2337-508f-92ae-92b8182116cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7897b954-a80d-5552-9b97-0e5fbd8e14e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469268} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd275cb-adea-5351-8c2d-fe4629e73b90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469269} :answer-field/id #uuid "90f7b91a-9437-57e9-a79f-e0b93efe37d8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "837117d8-f384-5bd9-a6ce-cc9066fb6bb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469270} {:answer/id #uuid "12466bb5-6322-58ca-959d-97ddedf72119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469271} :answer-field/id #uuid "c16860bd-48c3-55ea-a6e4-2951ea1c0825" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470247}] :question/id #uuid "eca92846-b208-5714-9d9f-4947d539dbcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-81819" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(4,4),(-3,-3),(-1,7).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n- **I.** $(3,-3)$\n- **II.** $(-4,-4)$\n- **III.** $(1,-7)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-4,-4),(3,3),(1,-7).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "713bf4d1-ab25-5361-9e9c-7d24f6109f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469356} {:answer/id #uuid "fca5df3a-3e5a-5e39-9a04-d3f319e7d84e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469357} :answer-field/id #uuid "00bfb755-07a7-5384-afe7-6f942d8cdae4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cedc26c-1cb4-5561-91be-d73dca72eab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469358} {:answer/id #uuid "5c31dbde-32b2-5234-9bd4-6944f689fadc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469358} :answer-field/id #uuid "a114cd92-2f22-5619-a9bb-e21a137ce0f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92b2e7d6-aa30-5b80-957f-c37f1213cfe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469360} {:answer/id #uuid "a6cebcec-f8a1-5f8f-855b-9e7e5f372074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469361} :answer-field/id #uuid "0719e008-e95e-5a2a-a79a-71437fdfac55" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470292}] :question/id #uuid "aecd389a-6729-5b9c-b536-b0ab5fd89940" :question/math-academy-id "q-8396" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(2,1),(3,3),(4,4).$  Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(-2,-1)$\n- **II.** $(-3,-2)$\n- **III.** $(-3,-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-2,-1),(-3,-3),(-4,-4).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092274 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092114 :question/id #uuid "7091b406-96d1-5663-9575-66f26c6a6267" :question/math-academy-id "e-7186" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a43a1658a16151c0306702959c50e8d0288077983ad50a084b39703e206469c0.png)\n\nConsider the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ shown above. Find the vector $A\\mathbf{v}$ given that \n![](images/ac/ac8c8fcdf75b72b65ceadb1d500625d4414264973876c10bf47c47a8e418ffd7.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j} \\}$ of the Euclidean plane $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of $\\{ \\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j} \\}$ under $A,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =Ai=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =Aj=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/41/414cb72ff004fe4c5898a0e2c7b60b4b3651473e776388fad21efd8fc9ae6165.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $A\\mathbf{v},$ we need to rotate $\\mathbf{v}$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b2/b24d8d460b7833a49f2bd7183f0f4b5d22d94a7d3b1d3bb9eb51beff9eeb7ef6.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4df33ff-e04e-55ec-b273-9eceff7db53b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88da30c2-feaa-5d94-9c98-e41fd1ed9ea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/09b2ae9333118de0621a5f29610b6a83689fadaeb9c05e7a30b2799b12a1bd58.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091163} {:answer/id #uuid "93a9126c-4c6c-5b2d-95c6-cfed9b180113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0d1ea82168dc6a122d1b20ad568b8958af496fc963edfb5e789bf57fc9108624.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091164} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9a95e0-ae9b-5161-a560-ee947bd76206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ab/abbe6cfa0d2f408bad937bb4beaa5cea011eec07e9201a8decbb6e25e734e568.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091165} {:answer/id #uuid "02bb3447-584b-5dae-af10-da7e71bffad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5a1923eec2b66ef