 we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $f(x)={x}^{3},$ $n=2,$ and $\\lambda =5.$\nSince $n=2,$ we need to compute the first $2-1=1$ derivatives of $f:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{3} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{2}(5)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(5) & {f}^{′}(5) \\\\ 0 & f(5)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{5}^{3} & 3\\cdot {5}^{2} \\\\ 0 & {5}^{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}125 & 75 \\\\ 0 & 125\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363595 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78d66bb7-295d-5426-85d5-ecc60dac6869" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363597} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a9dd6a1-550f-5ff1-ac0d-0d56b1c23d4f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363596} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a6b076b-e766-5c8f-a0cd-03e5ed12203c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363599} :answer-field/id #uuid "c21edd57-5874-58ec-99eb-20eab351adac" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363598} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "969f3547-f1ea-5d49-aedd-8aea07982cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363601} :answer-field/id #uuid "c69bc05e-3061-5ad4-a12b-c0cee73a6a62" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363600} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54767c70-f1e8-5c2a-9645-45bac744baa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363603} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2abb45a-5a37-5e8a-8dec-08ca46eb293c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59a6f51e-666c-56d3-ba03-4f7283a04750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363605} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b6eb381-0284-5836-85ce-d79a42d2b9b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "482359e7-082a-504d-bc57-f6163c9f176a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363607} :answer-field/id #uuid "61590ccc-fca1-55ef-a95d-40c03c2fae1e" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363606}] :question/id #uuid "290de3f9-01bf-5fef-a22f-da08c098a0ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-253323" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\operatorname{tan}⁡({J}_{3}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ $n=3,$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nSince $n=3,$ we need to compute the first $3-1=2$ derivative of $f:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{3}(\\pi )) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & {f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & \\frac{1}{2!}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ 0 & f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & {f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & {sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & {sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377004 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73a4b99c-267a-5cc8-9f5e-6d1d6494905e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377006}] :answer-fie