$8$ | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |\n|  | $0$ | $0$ | $27$ | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $27$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({J}_{2}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}(3))^{3} & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}{J}_{2}(2) & 0 \\\\ 0 & {J}_{2}(3)\\end{bmatrix})}^{3} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}({J}_{2}(2))^{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & ({J}_{2}(3))^{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =({J}_{2}(2))^{3}\\,⊕\\,({J}_{2}(3))^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the function of each Jordan block separately.\n\n- For ${J}_{2}(2),$ we have $n=2$ and $\\lambda =2.$ Since $n=2,$ we need to compute the first derivative of $f$ only:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{3} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{2}(2)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) \\\\ 0 & f(2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{2}^{3} & 3\\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\ 0 & {2}^{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For ${J}_{2}(3),$ we have $n=2$ and $\\lambda =3.$ Since $n=2,$ we need the first derivative of $f$ only, which we have already computed. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{2}(3)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(3) & {f}^{′}(3) \\\\ 0 & f(3)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{3}^{3} & 3\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\ 0 & {3}^{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}27 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 27\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n({J}_{2}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}(3))^{3}=({J}_{2}(2))^{3}\\,⊕\\,({J}_{2}(3))^{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 12 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 27 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 27\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "690f25cd-9fac-5812-aa86-851751150d08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291082} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e9b8079-a913-5e4d-92e6-d349f755d2ab" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291892} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "357699af-2b79-5d63-9e6a-60e4e15f1367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290849} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a92b88c-8254-5292-ae8f-90a1db4f8f48" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "537fa4f7-684e-55bc-8ed4-ec02685dae16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290987} :answer-field/id #uuid "859182e4-235f-5df0-83d9-d74e387e8cbf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1895e02e-cbf5-58b0-9b56-73c0b66223b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290734} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2981b54-bcf3-5ea2-b4e0-245d9a2cce3b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292374}] :question/id #uuid "5f9fe47a-1d49-50f6-9c5d-ebf149ad2b0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-253873" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | $3$ | {{field-1}} | $\\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2}$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${3}^{({J}_{3}(1)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(2))}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | $3$ | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |\n|  | $0$ | $0$ | $3$ | $0$ |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-4}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2({J}_{3}(1)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(2))} & ={3}^{(\\begin{bmatrix}{J}_{3}(1) & 0 \\\\ 0 & {J}_{1}(2)\\end{bmatrix})} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{3}^{({J}_{3}(1))} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {3}^{({J}_{1}(2))}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={3}^{({J}_{3}(1))}\\,⊕\\,{3}^{({J}_{1}(2))}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the function of each Jordan block separately.\n\n- For ${J}_{3}(1),$ we have $n=3$ and $\\lambda =2.$ Since $n=3,$ we need to compute the first and second derivative of $f$ only:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={3}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & ={3}^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{3}(1)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(1) & {f}^{′}(1) & \\frac{1}{2!}{f}^{″}(1) \\\\ 0 & f(1) & {f}^{′}(1) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{3}^{1} & {3}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {3}^{1}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2} \\\\ 0 & {3}^{1} & {3}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {3}^{1}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & \\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For ${J}_{1}(2),$ we have $n=1$ and $\\lambda =1.$ since $n=1,$ we don't need any derivatives. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{1}(2)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{3}^{(2)}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{({J}_{3}(1)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(2))} & ={3}^{({J}_{3}(1))}\\,⊕\\,{3}^{({J}_{1}(2))} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & \\frac{3}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292564 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f657dce0-5722-5f06-80b3-eaf633acd5c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291668} :answer-field/id #uuid "042ff51c-18e0-5237-b376-38f7930eb782" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c52cd005-01cf-5ff8-b591-fa149d221a54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291479} :answer-field/id #uuid "2708420c-b806-58ef-849a-5badb991dcba" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1b3f22c-ff9b-525d-883c-fec3572f7ff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291338} :answer-field/id #uuid "74e569bf-6689-5974-8361-858ba8a2b82c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a3df8b-4d67-5704-acac-5ba07b836156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290726} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbf5678a-2906-51bb-921c-fe3371a9d1fd" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292312} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3c7f034-4f58-54c2-a6ee-8e495bdef92f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291347} :answer-field/id #uuid "d245a96b-e14a-501d-8594-ac906984dc31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292372}] :question/id #uuid "a5aca3e1-68b3-5e91-9803-0207e7f29163" :question/math-academy-id "q-253877" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${({J}_{3}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(3))}^{4}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | $16$ | {{field-4}} | $0$ |  |\n|  | $0$ | $0$ | $16$ | $0$ |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-5}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({J}_{3}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(3))}^{4} & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}{J}_{3}(2) & 0 \\\\ 0 & {J}_{1}(3)\\end{bmatrix})}^{4} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{({J}_{3}(2))}^{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {({J}_{1}(3))}^{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={({J}_{3}(2))}^{4}\\,⊕\\,{({J}_{1}(3))}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the function of each Jordan block separately.\n\n- For ${J}_{3}(2),$ we have $n=3$ and $\\lambda =2.$ \\since $n=3,$ we need to compute the first and second derivatives of $f$ only:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{4} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =12{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{3}(2)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(2)}{2} \\\\ 0 & f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{2}^{4} & 4\\cdot {2}^{3} & \\frac{12\\cdot {2}^{2}}{2} \\\\ 0 & {2}^{4} & 4\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 & 32 & 24 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 32 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For ${J}_{1}(3),$ we have $n=1$ and $\\lambda =1.$ since $n=1,$ we don't need any derivatives. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{1}(3)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(3)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{3}^{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}81\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({J}_{3}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(3))}^{4} & ={({J}_{3}(2))}^{4}\\,⊕\\,{({J}_{1}(3))}^{4} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 & 32 & 24 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 32 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 81\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363654 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43be0bb3-7652-5157-9451-7bf833827379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363656} :answer-field/id #uuid "83740fd6-0ede-55a0-90dc-e8e21cddb2fa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53a724eb-5206-5811-ae45-2b13d8abb341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363658} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d9b417c-e1fc-56b2-9917-3684744860dd" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363657} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1bf7a1b-4455-59b5-bf37-ac01669259de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363660} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee5b6b53-b9a3-5ab7-8376-f23a3f4fce80" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363659} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a39c88d5-b67a-5d0a-871e-dea31d3cf9f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363662} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6ed2d02-a756-598c-8f1e-3b473ddaddbe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea28eb5d-45a1-5080-8f65-072597dd6c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363664} :answer-field/id #uuid "4db6f8f9-6a8b-5a6c-8713-0a6bd7bf7b38" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363663}] :question/id #uuid "ed4fc4e8-282a-5e85-aa0a-5e89ea16929e" :question/math-academy-id "q-253844" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${e}^{({J}_{2}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(1))}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | $0$ |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-5}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{({J}_{2}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(1))} & ={e}^{(\\begin{bmatrix}{J}_{2}(2) & 0 \\\\ 0 & {J}_{1}(1)\\end{bmatrix})} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{({J}_{2}(2))} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{({J}_{1}(1))}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{({J}_{2}(2))}\\,⊕\\,{e}^{({J}_{1}(1))}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the function of each Jordan block separately.\n\n- For ${J}_{2}(2),$ we have $n=2$ and $\\lambda =2.$ since $n=2,$ we need to compute the first derivative of $f$ only:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{2}(2)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) \\\\ 0 & f(2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2} & {e}^{2} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For ${J}_{1}(1),$ we have $n=1$ and $\\lambda =1.$ \\since $n=1,$ we don't need any derivatives. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{1}(1)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{(1)}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}e\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{({J}_{2}(1)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{2}(2))} & ={e}^{({J}_{2}(1))}\\,⊕\\,{e}^{({J}_{2}(2))} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2} & {e}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & e\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363665 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb8e620e-886a-5a0b-9d9d-d9bdfa4d5ba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363667} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9ec504b-fb6a-5444-8f81-11fc505d4f99" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0905b4db-4e18-5df8-b5cb-21a1e81e27c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363669} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5e14adc-7f18-5555-97a3-c03d46f5b0c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e763fae0-464a-57e3-a044-f1aed846aa47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363671} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a7b063b-cb64-5fcb-a8d2-4757b08ad643" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d28b6ce6-e19a-50ed-8aa9-2ee67515b28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363673} :answer-field/id #uuid "60e6c9eb-9501-5fab-82a7-68bcc32f55eb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63e1b279-556e-5e29-b829-e24cda7316d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363675} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6b584b2-296c-5858-8fec-57804a65c614" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363674}] :question/id #uuid "356147e0-2dde-55ac-9f10-6c69d5048d38" :question/math-academy-id "q-253890" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${({J}_{1}(3)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{3}(5))}^{2}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |\n|  | $0$ | $0$ | $25$ | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-5}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({J}_{1}(3)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{3}(5))}^{2} & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}{J}_{1}(3) & 0 \\\\ 0 & {J}_{3}(5)\\end{bmatrix})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{({J}_{1}(3))}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {({J}_{3}(5))}^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={({J}_{1}(3))}^{2}\\,⊕\\,{({J}_{3}(5))}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the function of each Jordan block separately.\n\n- For ${J}_{1}(3),$ we have $n=1$ and $\\lambda =3.$ since $n=1,$ we don't need any derivatives. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{1}(3)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(3)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{3}^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For ${J}_{3}(5),$ we have $n=3$ and $\\lambda =2.$ \\since $n=3,$ we need to compute the first and second derivatives of $f$ only:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =2x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{3}(5)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(5) & {f}^{′}(5) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(5)}{2} \\\\ 0 & f(5) & {f}^{′}(5) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(5)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{5}^{2} & 2\\cdot 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & {5}^{2} & 2\\cdot 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {5}^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 10 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 25 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 25\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({J}_{1}(3)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{3}(5)) & =({J}_{1}(3))\\,⊕\\,({J}_{3}(5)) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 25 & 10 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 25 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 25\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3f7e99e-94b4-5e9b-9bad-05d7b6014436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377015}] :answer-fiel